"""
Blue Pen (Windows)

What each tab really does:
  PC Game     - copies a game to a USB/external drive with a launcher that works,
                detects the game engine and applies that engine's real graphics options.
                Can also add a Linux launcher (.sh) that runs the game with Wine / Proton.
  Console     - puts a console game (your own dump) on the USB together with a portable
                emulator (DuckStation, PCSX2, RPCS3, Xenia) and a launcher, so it plays on any PC.
  Bootable    - turns a USB stick into a real UEFI-bootable stick from an ISO
                (Windows / Linux installers). ERASES the stick.
  Burn Disc   - checks whether an ISO is bootable and opens the Windows disc burner.
"""
